# OpenAxis — Backend Rules

## Route Handlers
- Use `async def` for ALL route handlers
- Each Node creates its own FastAPI app in `app.py`
- Use Pydantic models for all request/response schemas
- Validate all inputs at API boundaries — no raw dicts in route handlers

## Database
- Each Node owns its own DB — never shared between Nodes
- Use `from openaxis.core.db import create_db` to get an engine + session
- Use parameterized queries — never string-interpolate SQL
- Use `async with` for session management

## Auth (when needed)
- Use `Depends(get_current_user)` from `openaxis.core.auth`
- All financial actions must go through the Constitutional Gatekeeper before execution

## MCP Tools
- Every data-fetching function should also be decorated as an MCP tool
- Financial MCP tools must include "Requires human approval" in their docstring
- Use `@mcp_tool()` and `@mcp_resource()` from `openaxis.core.mcp`

## HTTP Clients
- Use `httpx.AsyncClient` for cross-Node REST calls
- Set timeouts — never fire-and-forget external HTTP calls without a timeout

## File Size
- No file over ~300 lines — split by concern (router.py, models.py, scraper.py, ranker.py, etc.)

## Error Handling
- Return structured error responses (Pydantic model), never raw strings
- Never expose stack traces in production responses
- Log actions via `openaxis.core.permissions.log_action` for audit trail

## Security
- Never store secrets in code — use env vars
- Rate-limit public endpoints
- Sanitize all external content before storing or returning
